.TH TMPFS 8
.SH NAME
tmpfs \- in-memory file system server
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmount \-t tmpfs \fR[\fB\-o \fIoptions\fR] \fBnone \fImountpoint
.SH DESCRIPTION
The tmpfs server keeps a file system in memory.
Its files, directories, symbolic links and device nodes are lost when it is
unmounted.
File data lives in pages that VM's cache shares, so files on tmpfs can be
mapped with
.BR mmap (2),
including writable MAP_SHARED mappings, and executed.
POSIX shared memory
.RB ( shm_open (3))
uses a tmpfs mounted on
.BR /var/shm .
.PP
The \fIoptions\fR field is a string of comma-delimited \fIkey\fB=\fIvalue\fR
options:
.TP 4
\fBsize=\fIbytes\fR[\fBk\fR|\fBm\fR|\fBg\fR]
The most file data the file system holds; by default, half of physical
memory.
Past that, writes fail with ENOSPC.
.TP
\fBnr_inodes=\fInumber\fR
The most files, directories and other nodes; by default, as many as there
are pages in \fBsize\fR.
.TP
\fBmode=\fIoctal\fR
The root directory's permissions; by default 1777.
.TP
\fBuid=\fInumber\fR, \fBgid=\fInumber\fR
The root directory's owner and group; by default 0.
.SH LIMITATIONS
File data is not paged out to swap, and file flags and extended attributes
are not supported.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR mount (8),
.BR mmap (2),
.BR shm_open (3)
